.TH "PB-ENV-INIT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-init - Create a password-protected ENV vault


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env init [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a password-protected ENV vault

.PP
Create password-protected local key custody for this account. Read the password from a private file or stdin; --recovery-file saves a newly generated recovery code to a new file. Already registered owned hosts receive an empty encrypted delivery without authorizing new names.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. The interactive picker separates shared Team globals, your private member globals, and device overrides in the active workspace; commands select exact scopes explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for init

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--password-file\fP=""
	read the raw master password from an absolute owner-only file

.PP
\fB--password-stdin\fP[=false]
	read the raw master password from non-interactive stdin

.PP
\fB--recovery-file\fP=""
	save a newly generated recovery code to a new absolute file path


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
